// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! kat_vectors -- real intermediate values from the HQC reference implementation
//! (gitlab.com/pqc-hqc/hqc, tag v5.0.0), extracted verbatim from
//! `kats/ref/hqc-1/intermediates_values` (shipped in-tree next to the official
//! `kats/ref/hqc-1/PQCkemKAT_2321.{req,rsp}` KAT files, generated by the same
//! release's `verbose` build mode -- see that file's own header: `N: 17669
//! N1: 46 N2: 384 OMEGA: 66 OMEGA_R: 75`, i.e. hqc-128/HQC-1).
//!
//! Fetched directly via `curl` from
//! https://gitlab.com/pqc-hqc/hqc/-/raw/v5.0.0/kats/ref/hqc-1/intermediates_values
//! (not through any summarizing/paraphrasing tool) and cross-checked
//! independently in Python (hashlib.sha3_512/shake_256) before being
//! transcribed into this file by a small script reading that same raw
//! download -- so there is no hand-retyped hex anywhere below.
//!
//! IMPORTANT: this `intermediates_values` file is a standalone illustrative
//! run (the reference's "verbose mode"), NOT tied to the KAT `.rsp`'s
//! count=0 vector's `seed` field -- the two use unrelated seeds (confirmed:
//! `seed_kem` below does NOT derive from the .rsp seed via `Prng`). That is
//! irrelevant for what this file is used for: verifying that our `Xof`/`Prng`/
//! `hashI`/`hashG`/sampler chain reproduces the reference's OWN chain, for
//! whatever seed it started from. Two independent chains are pinned:
//!
//!   1. keygen chain: seed_dk --Xof--> (y, x)  [same Xof context, y then x --
//!      this is what caught the `Xof.getBytes` 8-byte-rounding quirk, see
//!      prng.zig's module doc]; seed_ek --Xof--> h (SampleVect).
//!   2. hash chain: I(seed_pke) == seed_dk || seed_ek; G(H(ek_kem), m, salt)
//!      == K || theta.
//!
//! Both chains were independently re-derived in Python (hashlib) from this
//! same raw file before being ported to kat_test.zig -- see the session notes
//! in SPEC.md's Verification section.

